    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="lg_note" value="&lt;b&gt;All 67 relationships are 1:N.&lt;/b&gt; No FK column is UNIQUE, so the schema declares no 1:1. The junction tables whose two sides are both FK-enforced are composite_role, resource_scope, resource_policy, scope_policy and associated_policy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Not drawn:&lt;/b&gt; Keycloak enforces only part of its joins. Columns such as client.realm_id, user_entity.realm_id, keycloak_group.realm_id, client_scope.realm_id, *.role_id, *.group_id, *.scope_id and the whole fed_user_* / offline_* family carry no FK constraint, so no line is drawn for them. They are reported separately in the analysis.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hover a table, a column name or a line for the DDL detail (type, default, constraint and index names). After moving tables, select the lines and use Arrange → Clear Waypoints (Alt+Shift+R) to re-route them." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=11;fontColor=#334155;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="legend">
     <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1150" y="48" width="840" height="280" />
    </mxCell>
